  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 124 PM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nTuesday through Sunday:\n\nHigh pressure builds back in on Tuesday, with light winds and\nplenty of sunshine. Expect highs around 60 degrees. High pressure\nremains in place through Tuesday night, with increasing high\nclouds and light and variable to calm winds. A shortwave\npropagates southeastward through the northern Plains overnight\nTuesday, deepening a weak surface low and bringing showers across\nWisconsin throughout Wednesday. Minimal accumulations are\nexpected, generally up to 0.10 inch of precipitation are expected. \n\nThe surface low continues to deepen as it phases with a stream of\nGulf moisture crossing into the Mississippi Valley, allowing for\nincreasing northerly winds as the low exits and therefore precipitation\ntapers off Wednesday night. With steady northerly flow over Lake\nMichigan, a strong band of lake effect showers will develop. This\nband may wobble onshore inland over Lake Michigan counties at \ntimes Wednesday night all the way into Friday night as low\npressure continues to deepen in the mid-Atlantic and keeps strong\nnortherly winds in place through the aforementioned timeframe.\n\nGoing into Friday night, expecting low pressure to lift north into\nthe Northeast U.S. and therefore winds to shift to northwesterly,\nshutting off any remaining lake effect in southeastern Wisconsin.\nOverall, expecting rain to be the dominant version of\nprecipitation. However, inland temperatures Thursday and Friday\nnights are expected to fall into the mid to upper 20s, therefore\nallowing for some rain/snow mix, or perhaps even a period of pure\nsnow to fall if the band wobbles far enough inland. Areas near\nLake Michigan are expected to stay in rain to rain/snow mix due to\nthe lake temperatures remaining around 50 degrees and onshore\nflow keeping immediate lakeshore to immediately inland\ntemperatures above freezing (mid-30s to near 40 degrees). Daytime\ntemperatures in the 40s are expected Thursday through Saturday.\n\nBy Saturday, expect winds to diminish and skies to clear as low\npressure exits into the Atlantic Ocean. High pressure builds into\nthe region, clearing skies and bringing light winds through\nSunday. Expect highs around 50 degrees and dry conditions on\nSunday.\n\nMH",
